  "content": {
    "id": "p17-q4-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "4",
    "prompt": "Graphically find the set of values $x$ such that:",
    "layout": "grid",
    "columns": 2,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p17-q4-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "$(x-1)(x+5)\\ge0$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x\\le-5$ or $x\\ge1$.",
          "worked": "Let $y=(x-1)(x+5)$. The upward-opening parabola has $x$-intercepts $-5$ and $1$. It lies on or above the $x$-axis outside these intercepts, including both endpoints.\n\n$x\\le-5$ or $x\\ge1$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 55
      },
      {
        "id": "p17-q4-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$x(x-2)>0$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x<0$ or $x>2$.",
          "worked": "Let $y=x(x-2)$. The upward-opening parabola has $x$-intercepts $0$ and $2$. It lies above the $x$-axis outside these intercepts. Exclude both endpoints because the inequality is strict.\n\n$x<0$ or $x>2$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 55
      },
      {
        "id": "p17-q4-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "$x(3x-2)<0$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$0<x<\\dfrac23$.",
          "worked": "Let $y=x(3x-2)$. The upward-opening parabola has $x$-intercepts $0$ and $\\dfrac23$. It lies below the $x$-axis between these intercepts. Exclude both endpoints.\n\n$0<x<\\dfrac23$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 58
      },
      {
        "id": "p17-q4-d",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "$(x+2)(x+3)\\le0$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$-3\\le x\\le-2$.",
          "worked": "Let $y=(x+2)(x+3)$. The upward-opening parabola has $x$-intercepts $-3$ and $-2$. It lies on or below the $x$-axis between these intercepts, including both endpoints.\n\n$-3\\le x\\le-2$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 55
      },
      {
        "id": "p17-q4-e",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "e",
        "prompt": "$(x-3)(x-4)>0$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x<3$ or $x>4$.",
          "worked": "Let $y=(x-3)(x-4)$. The upward-opening parabola has $x$-intercepts $3$ and $4$. It lies above the $x$-axis outside these intercepts. Exclude both endpoints.\n\n$x<3$ or $x>4$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 55
      },
      {
        "id": "p17-q4-f",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "f",
        "prompt": "$(x-1)(2x+1)<0$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$-\\dfrac12<x<1$.",
          "worked": "Let $y=(x-1)(2x+1)$. The upward-opening parabola has $x$-intercepts $-\\dfrac12$ and $1$. It lies below the $x$-axis between these intercepts. Exclude both endpoints.\n\n$-\\dfrac12<x<1$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 58
      },
      {
        "id": "p17-q4-g",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "g",
        "prompt": "$x^2+6x+8\\ge0$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x\\le-4$ or $x\\ge-2$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}x^2+6x+8&=(x+2)(x+4).\\end{align*}$$\nThe graph of $y=x^2+6x+8$ opens upward and has $x$-intercepts $-4$ and $-2$. It lies on or above the $x$-axis outside these intercepts, including both endpoints.\n\n$x\\le-4$ or $x\\ge-2$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 62
      },
      {
        "id": "p17-q4-h",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "h",
        "prompt": "$x^2+7x-18\\le0$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$-9\\le x\\le2$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}x^2+7x-18&=(x+9)(x-2).\\end{align*}$$\nThe graph of $y=x^2+7x-18$ opens upward and has $x$-intercepts $-9$ and $2$. It lies on or below the $x$-axis between these intercepts, including both endpoints.\n\n$-9\\le x\\le2$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 62
      },
      {
        "id": "p17-q4-i",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "i",
        "prompt": "$3x^2+8x+4>0$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x<-2$ or $x>-\\dfrac23$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}3x^2+8x+4&=(3x+2)(x+2).\\end{align*}$$\nThe graph of $y=3x^2+8x+4$ opens upward and has $x$-intercepts $-2$ and $-\\dfrac23$. It lies above the $x$-axis outside these intercepts. Exclude both endpoints.\n\n$x<-2$ or $x>-\\dfrac23$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 65
      },
      {
        "id": "p17-q4-j",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "j",
        "prompt": "$2x^2+5x-3<0$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$-3<x<\\dfrac12$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}2x^2+5x-3&=(2x-1)(x+3).\\end{align*}$$\nThe graph of $y=2x^2+5x-3$ opens upward and has $x$-intercepts $-3$ and $\\dfrac12$. It lies below the $x$-axis between these intercepts. Exclude both endpoints.\n\n$-3<x<\\dfrac12$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 65
      },
      {
        "id": "p17-q4-k",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "k",
        "prompt": "$x^2+x\\ge6$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x\\le-3$ or $x\\ge2$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}x^2+x-6&\\ge0\\\\(x+3)(x-2)&\\ge0.\\end{align*}$$\nThe graph of $y=(x+3)(x-2)$ opens upward and has $x$-intercepts $-3$ and $2$. It lies on or above the $x$-axis outside these intercepts, including both endpoints.\n\n$x\\le-3$ or $x\\ge2$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 69
      },
      {
        "id": "p17-q4-l",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "l",
        "prompt": "$x^2\\le x+12$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$-3\\le x\\le4$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}x^2-x-12&\\le0\\\\(x-4)(x+3)&\\le0.\\end{align*}$$\nThe graph of $y=(x-4)(x+3)$ opens upward and has $x$-intercepts $-3$ and $4$. It lies on or below the $x$-axis between these intercepts, including both endpoints.\n\n$-3\\le x\\le4$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 69
      },
      {
        "id": "p17-q4-m",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "m",
        "prompt": "$(x+1)(x+2)>12$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x<-5$ or $x>2$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}(x+1)(x+2)-12&>0\\\\x^2+3x-10&>0\\\\(x+5)(x-2)&>0.\\end{align*}$$\nThe graph of $y=(x+5)(x-2)$ opens upward and has $x$-intercepts $-5$ and $2$. It lies above the $x$-axis outside these intercepts. Exclude both endpoints.\n\n$x<-5$ or $x>2$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 76
      },
      {
        "id": "p17-q4-n",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "n",
        "prompt": "$(x+1)(x-1)<2x$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$1-\\sqrt2<x<1+\\sqrt2$.\n\nThe upward-opening parabola is below the $x$-axis between its intercepts.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}(x+1)(x-1)-2x&<0\\\\x^2-2x-1&<0.\\end{align*}$$\nFor the intercepts of $y=x^2-2x-1$,\n$$\\begin{align*}x^2-2x-1&=(x-1)^2-2\\\\(x-1)^2&=2\\\\x&=1\\pm\\sqrt2.\\end{align*}$$\nThe parabola opens upward and lies below the $x$-axis between these intercepts. Exclude both endpoints.\n\n$1-\\sqrt2<x<1+\\sqrt2$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 90
      }
    ]
  },
